<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="spacing">
  <title>Spacing</title>
  <shortdesc>Use margin and padding utilities to quickly control the layout of elements. The <xmlatt
    >margin</xmlatt> and <xmlatt
    >padding</xmlatt> attributes enable standard Bootstrap spacing across a range of DITA components.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Spacing</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Margin</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Padding</indexterm>
        <indexterm>CSS
          <indexterm><xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt></indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlatt>margin</xmlatt></indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlatt>padding</xmlatt></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body outputclass="language-markup">
    <section>
      <title>Margin</title>
      <p>The <xmlatt
        >margin</xmlatt> attribute controls the distance between elements, supporting values from 0 to 5 and <codeph
        >auto</codeph>.</p>
    </section>

    <bodydiv outputclass="p-3 border">
      <div outputclass="m-0 p-2 text-bg-primary">Margin 0</div>
      <div outputclass="m-1 p-2 text-bg-secondary">Margin 1</div>
      <div outputclass="m-2 p-2 text-bg-success">Margin 2</div>
      <div outputclass="m-3 p-2 text-bg-danger">Margin 3</div>
      <div outputclass="m-4 p-2 text-bg-warning">Margin 4</div>
      <div outputclass="m-5 p-2 text-bg-info">Margin 5</div>
      <div outputclass="m-auto p-2 w-50 text-bg-light">Margin Auto</div>
    </bodydiv>

    <codeblock><coderef href="code/spacing/margin.xml"/></codeblock>

    <section>
      <title>Padding</title>
      <p>The <xmlatt
        >padding</xmlatt> attribute controls the internal spacing of an element, supporting values from 0 to 5.</p>
    </section>

    <bodydiv outputclass="p-3 border">
      <div outputclass="p-0 text-bg-primary">Padding 0</div>
      <div outputclass="m-1 p-1 text-bg-secondary"><div
          outputclass="bg-secondary-subtle text-dark w-100"
        >Padding 1</div></div>
      <div outputclass="m-1 p-2 text-bg-success"><div
          outputclass="bg-success-subtle text-dark w-100"
        >Padding 2</div></div>
      <div outputclass="m-1 p-3 text-bg-danger"><div
          outputclass="bg-danger-subtle text-dark w-100"
        >Padding 3</div></div>
      <div outputclass="m-1 p-4 text-bg-warning"><div
          outputclass="bg-warning-subtle text-dark w-100"
        >Padding 4</div></div>
      <div outputclass="m-1 p-5 text-bg-info"><div outputclass="bg-info-subtle text-dark w-100">Padding 5</div></div>
    </bodydiv>

    <codeblock><coderef href="code/spacing/padding.xml"/></codeblock>

    <section>
      <title>Directional Spacing</title>
      <p>The <xmlatt>margin</xmlatt> and <xmlatt
        >padding</xmlatt> attributes also support directional spacing using a prefix:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><codeph>t</codeph> - Top</li>
        <li><codeph>b</codeph> - Bottom</li>
        <li><codeph>s</codeph> - Start (Left in LTR)</li>
        <li><codeph>e</codeph> - End (Right in LTR)</li>
        <li><codeph>x</codeph> - Horizontal (Start and End)</li>
        <li><codeph>y</codeph> - Vertical (Top and Bottom)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Multiple values can be specified as a space-separated list.</p>
    </section>

    <bodydiv outputclass="p-3 border">
      <div outputclass="mt-5 mb-0 text-bg-primary">Margin Top 5, Bottom 0</div>
      <div outputclass="mx-3 text-bg-secondary">Margin Horizontal 3</div>
      <div outputclass="py-5 text-bg-success"><div
          outputclass="bg-success-subtle text-dark w-100"
        >Padding Vertical 5</div></div>
      <div outputclass="ps-3 pe-1 text-bg-danger"><div
          outputclass="bg-danger-subtle text-dark w-100"
        >Padding Start 3, End 1</div></div>
    </bodydiv>

    <codeblock><coderef href="code/spacing/directional-spacing.xml"/></codeblock>
  </body>
</topic>
